-- txt --
# Usage
  rex        [--quiet-boot]          open the board (--quiet-boot: no sounds)
  rex        <command> -h            flags and examples for a command

# Start & steer
  new        [flags] -- <prompt>     start an agent session
  attach     <sel>                   open a session (ctrl+] detaches)
  reply      <sel> -- <text>         answer a session that needs input
  send       <sel> -- <text>         send raw input (stdin when no text)
  wait       <sel> -until STATE      block until a session reaches a state
  loop       start|ls|stop|…         re-send a prompt until a check passes
  here                               open this workspace's board

# Watch
  ls         [-state S] [-tool T]    list sessions
  status                             counts; exit 1 if one needs input
  log        <sel> [-f] [-n N]       print a session's transcript
  overview                           one-screen summary by bucket
  usage      [-range R] [-by model]  tokens, cost and plan quota
  digest                             today's sessions, time and totals
  stats                              lifetime usage by model and tool
  audit      [-since D] [-all]       one line per finished session
  errors     [-n N] [-clear]         failed rex commands

# Manage
  name       <sel> [-- <text>]       set, show or clear the display name
  rename     <sel> <slug>            change a session's slug
  done       <sel> [-after 72h]      mark done; cleared after retire_after_hours
  undone     <sel>                   cancel a pending done
  complete   <sel>                   stop a session now and mark it done
  resume     <sel> [-print]          respawn an exited session
  undo       <sel> [-turns N]        restore the folder to before the last turn
  redo       <sel>                   bring back what undo replaced
  archive    <sel>                   archive a session
  rm         <sel> [-force]          delete a session
  prune      [-dry-run] [-yes]       delete Completed sessions
  fleet      ls|show|set|unset       list or edit session fleets
  export     <sel>                   write a session as a readable document

# Daemon
  daemon     start|stop|restart|…    manage rex-daemon (also status, logs)
  reload                             reload tools.yaml, config and Lua
  upgrade    [-cold] [-yes]          hot-restart onto a newly installed build

# Setup
  setup      [-yes]                  first-run wizard
  onboard                            guided tour: checks, agents, keys
  doctor                             check the install; exit 1 if a check fails
  config     list|get|set|reset|…    view and change settings
  theme      list|show|new           list, inspect and create color themes
  trust      [dir] [-ls] [-rm dir]   trust a folder so agents skip its dialog
  ws         init|ls|open|…          workspaces (needs workspaces)
  skills                             list the skills library
  update     [-check]                upgrade rex in place
  uninstall  [-all] [-dry-run]       remove rex and optional state
  completion bash|zsh|fish           print a shell completion script
  render                             render an event stream from stdin
  version                            print the version
  agent-help                         the usage card for LLM agents

# Options
  <sel>                              short id (4+ hex), slug or full id
  -o         FORMAT                  text|txt|md|json|agent; txt when piped
  --agent                            one line per record, no color, no prompts
  --no-color                         never emit ANSI color
  agents     rex agent-help          the usage card for LLM agents
-- md --
### rex dev · Runtime Executive for Agents

#### Usage

| Name | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `rex [--quiet-boot]` | open the board (--quiet-boot: no sounds) |
| `rex <command> -h` | flags and examples for a command |

#### Start & steer

| Name | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `new [flags] -- <prompt>` | start an agent session |
| `attach <sel>` | open a session (ctrl+\] detaches) |
| `reply <sel> -- <text>` | answer a session that needs input |
| `send <sel> -- <text>` | send raw input (stdin when no text) |
| `wait <sel> -until STATE` | block until a session reaches a state |
| `loop start|ls|stop|…` | re-send a prompt until a check passes |
| `here` | open this workspace's board |

#### Watch

| Name | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `ls [-state S] [-tool T]` | list sessions |
| `status` | counts; exit 1 if one needs input |
| `log <sel> [-f] [-n N]` | print a session's transcript |
| `overview` | one-screen summary by bucket |
| `usage [-range R] [-by model]` | tokens, cost and plan quota |
| `digest` | today's sessions, time and totals |
| `stats` | lifetime usage by model and tool |
| `audit [-since D] [-all]` | one line per finished session |
| `errors [-n N] [-clear]` | failed rex commands |

#### Manage

| Name | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `name <sel> [-- <text>]` | set, show or clear the display name |
| `rename <sel> <slug>` | change a session's slug |
| `done <sel> [-after 72h]` | mark done; cleared after retire\_after\_hours |
| `undone <sel>` | cancel a pending done |
| `complete <sel>` | stop a session now and mark it done |
| `resume <sel> [-print]` | respawn an exited session |
| `undo <sel> [-turns N]` | restore the folder to before the last turn |
| `redo <sel>` | bring back what undo replaced |
| `archive <sel>` | archive a session |
| `rm <sel> [-force]` | delete a session |
| `prune [-dry-run] [-yes]` | delete Completed sessions |
| `fleet ls|show|set|unset` | list or edit session fleets |
| `export <sel>` | write a session as a readable document |

#### Daemon

| Name | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `daemon start|stop|restart|…` | manage rex-daemon (also status, logs) |
| `reload` | reload tools.yaml, config and Lua |
| `upgrade [-cold] [-yes]` | hot-restart onto a newly installed build |

#### Setup

| Name | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `setup [-yes]` | first-run wizard |
| `onboard` | guided tour: checks, agents, keys |
| `doctor` | check the install; exit 1 if a check fails |
| `config list|get|set|reset|…` | view and change settings |
| `theme list|show|new` | list, inspect and create color themes |
| `trust [dir] [-ls] [-rm dir]` | trust a folder so agents skip its dialog |
| `ws init|ls|open|…` | workspaces (needs workspaces) |
| `skills` | list the skills library |
| `update [-check]` | upgrade rex in place |
| `uninstall [-all] [-dry-run]` | remove rex and optional state |
| `completion bash|zsh|fish` | print a shell completion script |
| `render` | render an event stream from stdin |
| `version` | print the version |
| `agent-help` | the usage card for LLM agents |

#### Options

| Name | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `<sel>` | short id (4+ hex), slug or full id |
| `-o FORMAT` | text\|txt\|md\|json\|agent; txt when piped |
| `--agent` | one line per record, no color, no prompts |
| `--no-color` | never emit ANSI color |
| `agents rex agent-help` | the usage card for LLM agents |
